is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: leaf_router_0_1
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: FRR BGP configuration on leaf_router_0_1. The BGP neighbor stanzas toward both spines are missing on the leaf.

Mechanism: With no BGP neighbors configured on leaf_router_0_1, no EBGP sessions can form to the spines. As a result, 10.0.1.0/24 is not advertised into the fabric, and the leaf learns no routes back to 10.0.0.0/24. From pc_0_1, pings to 10.0.0.2 get “Destination Net Unreachable” from 10.0.1.1 (the leaf), because the leaf has no route to 10.0.0.0/24.

Localization: 
- On the spines, “show ip bgp summary” shows neighbors 172.16.0.7 and 172.16.0.11 (the leaf-facing IPs) in Active state (no session).
- On leaf_router_0_1, “show ip bgp summary” returns “No BGP neighbors found,” and the running config contains only “router bgp 65201” with “network 10.0.1.0/24” and no neighbor lines.
- Leaf routing table contains only connected routes (10.0.1.0/24, 172.16.0.6/31, 172.16.0.10/31), confirming no BGP-learned prefixes.

Root cause: A recent configuration cleanup on leaf_router_0_1 removed the BGP neighbor statements to both spines.

Corrective fix: Recreate BGP neighbors on leaf_router_0_1:
- router bgp 65201
  neighbor 172.16.0.6 remote-as 65100  (to spine_router_0_0 over eth0)
  neighbor 172.16.0.10 remote-as 65101 (to spine_router_0_1 over eth1)
Keep the existing “network 10.0.1.0/24.” After committing, BGP sessions should establish and reachability between pc_0_1 and pc_0_0 will be restored.
=== END ===